These adaptations are distributed under the GNU Lesser General Public License,
version 2.1 or (at your option) any later version. The license text is included
in LGPL-2.1 in this directory. The adaptations use Go strings and bounded,
cancelable work instead of the original C data structures; patch subdivision
keeps the existing explicit work limit instead of introducing an approximate
result when that limit is exhausted. Blame uses a separate matcher.

Reference source: https://github.com/git/git/blob/master/xdiff/xdiffi.c
